{
  "company_name": "RefineCapital Systems",
  "industry": "Oil & Gas Refining",
  "use_case": "Working capital and cash flow optimization for oil & gas refining operations",
  "space_title": "RefineCapital Systems - Working Capital & Cash Flow Optimization 💰",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Oil & Gas Refining\n\n**Use case:** Working Capital & Cash Flow Optimization\n\nRefineCapital Systems — working capital and cash flow analytics across 20 business units spanning Processing, Supply Chain, Support, and Corporate segments. CFOs and Treasurers use this space to compress the cash conversion cycle, manage Days Sales Outstanding (DSO) and Days Payable Outstanding (DPO) against integrated-refiner benchmarks, and free up trapped working capital from inventory and receivables. Treasury teams use it for daily cash positioning and net debt management.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Cash conversion cycle (days) — refining peers typically run 15-40 days NWC\n- Days Sales Outstanding (DSO) — integrated refiners target 25-35 days\n- Days Payable Outstanding (DPO) — typically 30-50 days\n- Free cash flow ($) by segment\n- Current ratio — healthy refiners run 1.2-1.8\n- Net debt ($) and net debt / EBITDA leverage\n- Inventory tied up in feedstock and product (bbl converted to $)\n- Net cash flow (inflows − outflows) by business unit\n\n**Data sources**\n- `cash_transactions` — daily cash inflows and outflows by flow type and counterparty\n- `working_capital_snapshots` — weekly AR / AP / inventory / cash balances and DSO/DPO\n- `cashflow_monthly` — monthly FCF, cash conversion cycle, current ratio, net debt",
  "schema_basename": "og_refining_cashflow",
