  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Working Capital & Cash Flow Optimization for a refining business with Processing, Supply Chain, Support, and Corporate segments across Gulf Coast, Midwest, and National regions. Stakeholders include the CFO (FCF, cash conversion cycle, net debt), Treasurer (daily cash position, DSO/DPO, current ratio), and Segment VPs (segment-level NWC and FCF drivers).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Cash conversion cycle = cash_conversion_cycle_days on cashflow_monthly; integrated refiners typically run 15-40 days NWC\n- DSO = dso_days on working_capital_snapshots; integrated-refiner benchmark 25-35 days\n- DPO = dpo_days; benchmark 30-50 days; higher DPO = better working capital position (within supplier-risk limits)\n- Net working capital (NWC) = accounts_receivable_usd + inventory_usd - accounts_payable_usd\n- Free cash flow = free_cash_flow_usd; primary lens for dividend / buyback / capex allocation\n- Current ratio = current_ratio; healthy refiners run 1.2-1.8, <1.0 signals liquidity stress\n- Net debt = net_debt_usd; refining peers target net debt / EBITDA < 2.0x mid-cycle\n- Flow types: Collection (inflow), Disbursement (outflow), Intercompany, Tax Payment, Dividend\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - cash_transactions_metrics (source: cash_transactions) — dims: transaction_date, business_unit_id, segment, region, flow_type; measures: total_inflows_usd, total_outflows_usd, net_cash_flow_usd, total_transactions, max_amount, total_days_outstanding.\n  - working_capital_snapshots_metrics (source: working_capital_snapshots) — dims: snapshot_date, business_unit_id, segment, region; measures: total_receivables_usd, total_payables_usd, total_cash_balance_usd, avg_dso_days, total_inventory, total_dpo_days, max_accounts_receivable.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. business_unit_name, dso_days at row level, dpo_days at row level, free_cash_flow_usd, current_ratio, net_debt_usd).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
